{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    /*
      No DOM: every web global this package names — `fetch`, `Response`, `AbortSignal`, `URL` — is read from
      `@types/node` (undici-types), which is also the flavour `tencent-doc-sdk` compiles against. Adding DOM
      would bind a second, browser-shaped declaration over each of those names, and would additionally need
      `DOM.Iterable` before `FetcherHeaders`' iterator members exist at all.
      This is no longer about the transport seam. The seam is `WebFetcher` from `universal-fetch-type`, whose
      request body is DOM-compatible, so a DOM program can hand in its own `fetch` unwrapped — that direction
      is judged by `tests/xiv-datamine-polyfill-e2e-test/test/fetcher-variance.ts`, not by this file.
    */
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    /* `@/…` 是 `src/` 下的模块；别名在 vite.config.ts 里为 vite 声明，vitest 与打包走的就是它。声明由
       `unplugin-dts` 在打包同趟生成、自行解析别名——若用 tsc 直接 emit，`@/…` 会原样进声明，消费方读不到。 */
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    },
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,

    /* tsc -b 的增量状态文件。 */
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.app.tsbuildinfo"
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.json"]
}
